# Flash Cards
// A deck of cards to learn from:  a Spanish word on the front, what it means on the back.
// Click the card, or Show the answer, to turn it over, then say whether you knew it:
// the score keeps count, and the next card comes up at random.
// The card is this project's own, in `FlashCard.spell`;  this file holds the quiz, and its words.

quiz is an app:
	- its "deck" is a new deck
	// The card showing
	- its "card" is a flash card
	// How many you knew
	- its "known" is a number
	// How many you've tried
	- its "tried" is a number
	// Said in the toolbar
	- its "score" is:
		"Nothing tried yet" if the tried is 0
		"[known] of [tried] right" otherwise

	- group "playing"
	// A card from the deck at random, word up:  never the one just shown
	- to deal a card:
		set others to cards in the deck where it is not the card of quiz
		set the card to a random card in others
		turn the card face up
	- to show the answer:
		- titled "Show the answer"
		- shortcut space
		turn the card over
	// Counted, then the next card
	- to say i knew it:
		- titled "I knew it"
		- icon "check"
		- shortcut Y
		set the known to the known + 1
		set the tried to the tried + 1
		deal a card
	- to say i missed it:
		- titled "I missed it"
		- icon "close"
		- shortcut N
		set the tried to the tried + 1
		deal a card
	- to start over:
		- titled "Start over"
		- icon "redo"
		clear the known
		clear the tried
		deal a card
	- its "quiz menu" is a menu of "start over"

	// The toolbar with the score, the card, then what you can do:  turn it over, or say how you did
	- to draw it:
		<ui-container text>
			<ui-stack>
				<ui-toolbar menu="quiz menu" aria-label="Quiz">
					<ui-text slot="title" size="large">Flash Cards</ui-text>
					<ui-text slot="right">{the score}</ui-text>
				</ui-toolbar>
				{draw the card}
				<ui-stack direction="horizontal" justify="center">
					<if the card is face up>
						<ui-button color="primary" onClick={show the answer}>Show the answer</ui-button>
					<otherwise>
						<ui-button color="positive" icon="check" onClick={say i knew it}>I knew it</ui-button>
						<ui-button color="negative" appearance="basic" icon="close" onClick={say i missed it}>I missed it</ui-button>
					</otherwise>
				</ui-stack>
			</ui-stack>
		</ui-container>

## The deck:  twelve Spanish words -- add your own

to add (word as text) meaning (meaning as text):
	add (a new flash card with word = the word, meaning = the meaning) to quiz's deck

add "el gato" meaning "the cat"
add "el perro" meaning "the dog"
add "la casa" meaning "the house"
add "el libro" meaning "the book"
add "la manzana" meaning "the apple"
add "el agua" meaning "the water"
add "la luna" meaning "the moon"
add "el sol" meaning "the sun"
add "la playa" meaning "the beach"
add "el tren" meaning "the train"
add "la llave" meaning "the key"
add "la mariposa" meaning "the butterfly"

start over
